# Website Convention Rules

## Brand palette
Canonical hex values live in `src/constants/brandColors.js` (also `tailwind` `brand.*`). Prefer semantic utilities, not arbitrary hex:

- Page / shell: `bg-brand-dark`, `from-brand-dark` (gradients)
- CTAs and accents: `bg-brand-orange`, `hover:bg-brand-orange-dark`, `text-brand-orange`, `border-brand-orange`, `shadow-brand-orange/30`
- Gradient headlines: class `text-gradient` (see `src/index.css`)
- Font: `Inter` only (`font-sans`)

Inline styles are only for dynamic tints that depend on per-item data (e.g. catalog cards); use `BRAND_ORANGE` from `brandColors.js` as the base color.

## Section order (must not change)
Navbar → Hero → About → ClientLogos → Catalog → Pricing → Contact → Footer

## Icons
- Use **Lucide React** only: `import { IconName } from 'lucide-react'`
- No emoji in UI, no custom SVG unless it's the logo
- Logo: `<img src="/images/stand-logo.png" />`

## CTA
```jsx
<a href="https://playstand.app/login" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
  Empezar gratis
</a>
```
Always `target="_blank"` with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`

## Hard rules
- **No TypeScript** — all files are .jsx, never .tsx or .ts
- **No React Router** — single page, sections scroll into view
- **No auth code** — website has zero authentication
- **No new npm packages** unless absolutely necessary
- Custom class `bg-glass` in `src/index.css` — use for frosted navbar when scrolled
- Tailwind 3.4.4 only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
